## 9. functions/lib/videoCatalog.js — slugFromUrl (exact)

```js
/**
 * Derives a slug from a video URL filename.
 * e.g. "https://.../ugc 1.mp4" → "ugc-1"
 * @param {string} url
 * @returns {string}
 */
function slugFromUrl(url) {
  try {
    const pathname = new URL(url).pathname;
    const filename = decodeURIComponent(pathname.split('/').pop() || '');
    return filename
      .replace(/\.\w+$/, '')          // strip extension
      .replace(/\s+/g, '-')           // spaces → hyphens
      .replace(/[^a-zA-Z0-9-]/g, '')  // strip non-alphanumeric/hyphen
      .toLowerCase();
  } catch {
    return '';
  }
}
```
`slugFromUrl` is **module-private (not exported)**. Exported functions: `getAllVideos(request)`, `getVideosByCategory(request, categorySlug)`, `getVideoBySlug(request, slug)`. Each returned video carries `{ slug, url, category, label }` where `slug = slugFromUrl(url)`.

**IMPORTANT for client-side work:** To match server slugs client-side, `script.js` would need to replicate this exact transformation (URL pathname → filename → strip ext → spaces to hyphens → strip non-`[a-zA-Z0-9-]` → lowercase). Currently `script.js` does NOT compute slugs anywhere — `createReelCard` only stores the raw URL in the `<source data-src>`. The search index stores `{ title, video, category }` with no slug. So adding engagement tracking requires either (a) replicating `slugFromUrl` in JS, or (b) fetching slugs from `/api/videos`.

